{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":60894,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"b22392690ccac2b0c37bddd2435b655e","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; I have finally finished, and mailed, my boarding pass save the dates! I am so excited! These took a lot of work, and a lot of hours, but in the end it was all worth it! I got the template for the boarding passes from Ayleebits.com: (&lt;img height=\"16\" id=\"yui_3_3_0_8_130386016056229\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/cheesy.gif\" width=\"16\" \/&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;I entered all the pictures and the information myself on the template I got from Aylee using MS Word.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; When I was done with the template, I downloaded our guestlist\/address book into a MS Excel document then created a mail merge in MS Word. I also downloaded a bunch of different fonts from &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/www.dafont.com\"&gt;www.dafont.com&lt;\/a&gt; (Minya Nouvelle, Champignon, A Yummy Apology, Tropicana BV for the shapes like a starfish is P) I also got a few from &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/kevinandamanda.com\/fonts\/fontsforpeas\/\"&gt;http:\/\/kevinandamanda.com\/fonts\/fontsforpeas\/&lt;\/a&gt;. I really like both of those sites for fonts. The fonts for peas fonts are a little difficult to use due to spacing issues. Some of the handwriting fonts need to be such a large size, that they end up taking up the entire page of your boarding pass.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; My boarding pass was four pages. We requested a \u00e2\u20ac\u0153tentative RSVP\u00e2\u20ac\u009d since we need to get an idea of who all thinks the trip to Mexico for our wedding will be in their budget. I made the last page the RSVP and designed our own return label to attach to both the outer envelope and the back of the boarding pass, so the final page could be detached and sent back like a postcard (of course a stamp was on there too). If I were to do it over again, I would do the \u00e2\u20ac\u0153tentative RSVP\u00e2\u20ac\u009d differently. I had to buy stamps for all 66 invitations to be sent out ($0.81) and to attach to the return card ($0.44), so for all 66 invitations, we spent about $85! Ouch &lt;span alt=\":msncry:\" id=\"yui_3_3_0_8_130386016056252\" rel=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/msncry.gif\"&gt;&lt;img height=\"19\" id=\"yui_3_3_0_8_130386016056251\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/msncry.gif\" width=\"19\" \/&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;. Mistake! I have designed a webpage for our wedding (mikeandmandywedding.org) and there is an RSVP link that I should\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ve put on the boarding pass, instead of using a return postcard-that\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s my advice for future brides!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; So, back to the design of the boarding pass\u00e2\u20ac\u00a6I purchased white shimmer cardstock, and cream rectangle envelopes from paperandmore.com, then also went to Archivers and bought blue, teal, green, and coral shimmer cardstock for the boarding pass holder. (total spent on supplies (using coupons for cardstock at archivers) was $67.43. I purchased the Raffia, and ribbon from Michaels (about $3 each) and borrowed the supplies to emboss the boarding pass&amp;nbsp;ticket jackets&amp;nbsp;from my future mother in law. I used the template #2 (ayleebits.com again) and cut out my own version of the ticket jacket. I used sand stamps with golden sand embossing powder, and a blue\/teal mixture of embossing powder for the seashells. I also put rhinestones on the outer&amp;nbsp;jacket&amp;nbsp;and the boarding pass front page.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Kinkos was my second home for the cutting process. I took my white metallic cardstock and my thumb drive to Kinkos and printed 66 invitations onto the cardstock costing me about $13. Then they cut them for me into boarding pass sizes, and my Mom and I spent DAYS rounding the corners and cutting out the notches! Once they were all cut out, I used a special grommet tool, and put a grommet in the corner to hold the 4 pages together. Then tied a ribbon through the grommet, inserted the boarding passes into the ticket jacket, and put them in an outer cream envelope and tied them with Raffia. For the labels, I had purchased the clear mailing labels from paperandmore.com, so I used my mail merge to print out each address, and my return address, and mailed them out! That\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s it!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; To summarize the supplies I used:&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; 100 sheets White shimmer cardstock (&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/www.paperandmore.com) &amp;nbsp;66\"&gt;www.paperandmore.com) &lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;\/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; 66&amp;nbsp;sheets blue, green, aqua, coral shimmer cardstock (Archivers $0.59\/sheet, email coupons)&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;\/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; Kinkos printing and cutting services ($0.19\/print on my paper, free cutting because I batted my eyelashes &lt;span alt=\":mswink:\" id=\"yui_3_3_0_8_130386016056263\" rel=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/msnwink.gif\"&gt;&lt;img height=\"19\" id=\"yui_3_3_0_8_130386016056262\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/msnwink.gif\" width=\"19\" \/&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;\/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; Wet Embossing powder in blue\/teal, and golden sand (found at Archivers for $5 each)&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;\/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; 3 stamps-Seashells, Sand, and a \u00e2\u20ac\u0153handmade with love\u00e2\u20ac\u009d stamp all found at Archivers ($7 each)&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;\/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; Embossing gun (looks like a blowdryer, but heats to ridiculous strength! Careful!&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;\/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt; Last I used sticky rhinestones,&amp;nbsp;Raffia, and Ribbon&amp;nbsp;from Michaels.&lt;\/li&gt; &lt;\/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; This is the Boarding pass ticket jacket. Embossed with Teal\/Blue, and golden sand embossing powder (looks so real if you add a touch of teal to it!)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394712\/width\/1000\/height\/800\"&gt;&lt;img alt=\"Boarding pass ticket jacket 1\" height=\"343\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394712\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" width=\"476\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Another closer view of the ticket jacket.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\"Boarding pass ticket jacket 2\" height=\"332\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394714\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" style=\"width: 553px; height: 378px\" width=\"453\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; The inside of the ticket jacket.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\"Inside jacket \" height=\"335\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394716\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" style=\"width: 522px; height: 359px\" width=\"443\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; The Boarding Pass itself!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Page 1) Save the Date, Pack a bag\u00e2\u20ac\u00a6.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Page 2) Booking information\/Travel agent information&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Page 3)Traveling information (passports, hotel website, dates)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Page 4) Tentative RSVP \u00e2\u20ac\u201cWe\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re on board or not\u00e2\u20ac\u00a6&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\"Page 1 Boarding pass STD\" height=\"356\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394719\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" style=\"width: 563px; height: 343px\" width=\"503\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Page 2)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\"Page 2 Boarding pass STD\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394721\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Page 3)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\"Page 3 Boarding pass STD\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394723\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Page 4)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img alt=\"Page 4 Boarding pass STD\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394725\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/&gt;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Okay!&amp;nbsp; That&#039;s it for now...on to the next DIY project!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1441443,"PostDate":1303843588,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> I have finally finished, and mailed, my boarding pass save the dates! I am so excited! These took a lot of work, and a lot of hours, but in the end it was all worth it! I got the template for the boarding passes from Ayleebits.com: (<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' height=\"16\" id=\"yui_3_3_0_8_130386016056229\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/cheesy.gif\" width=\"16\" \/><\/span><\/span>\u00a0I entered all the pictures and the information myself on the template I got from Aylee using MS Word.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> When I was done with the template, I downloaded our guestlist\/address book into a MS Excel document then created a mail merge in MS Word. I also downloaded a bunch of different fonts from <a href='http:\/\/www.dafont.com' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>www.dafont.com<\/a> (Minya Nouvelle, Champignon, A Yummy Apology, Tropicana BV for the shapes like a starfish is P) I also got a few from <a href='http:\/\/kevinandamanda.com\/fonts\/fontsforpeas\/' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/kevinandamand...s\/fontsforpeas\/<\/a>. I really like both of those sites for fonts. The fonts for peas fonts are a little difficult to use due to spacing issues. Some of the handwriting fonts need to be such a large size, that they end up taking up the entire page of your boarding pass.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> My boarding pass was four pages. We requested a \u00e2\u20ac\u0153tentative RSVP\u00e2\u20ac\u009d since we need to get an idea of who all thinks the trip to Mexico for our wedding will be in their budget. I made the last page the RSVP and designed our own return label to attach to both the outer envelope and the back of the boarding pass, so the final page could be detached and sent back like a postcard (of course a stamp was on there too). If I were to do it over again, I would do the \u00e2\u20ac\u0153tentative RSVP\u00e2\u20ac\u009d differently. I had to buy stamps for all 66 invitations to be sent out ($0.81) and to attach to the return card ($0.44), so for all 66 invitations, we spent about $85! Ouch <span alt=\":msncry:\" id=\"yui_3_3_0_8_130386016056252\" rel=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/msncry.gif\"><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' height=\"19\" id=\"yui_3_3_0_8_130386016056251\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/msncry.gif\" width=\"19\" \/><\/span><\/span>. Mistake! I have designed a webpage for our wedding (mikeandmandywedding.org) and there is an RSVP link that I should\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ve put on the boarding pass, instead of using a return postcard-that\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s my advice for future brides!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> So, back to the design of the boarding pass\u00e2\u20ac\u00a6I purchased white shimmer cardstock, and cream rectangle envelopes from paperandmore.com, then also went to Archivers and bought blue, teal, green, and coral shimmer cardstock for the boarding pass holder. (total spent on supplies (using coupons for cardstock at archivers) was $67.43. I purchased the Raffia, and ribbon from Michaels (about $3 each) and borrowed the supplies to emboss the boarding pass\u00a0ticket jackets\u00a0from my future mother in law. I used the template #2 (ayleebits.com again) and cut out my own version of the ticket jacket. I used sand stamps with golden sand embossing powder, and a blue\/teal mixture of embossing powder for the seashells. I also put rhinestones on the outer\u00a0jacket\u00a0and the boarding pass front page.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Kinkos was my second home for the cutting process. I took my white metallic cardstock and my thumb drive to Kinkos and printed 66 invitations onto the cardstock costing me about $13. Then they cut them for me into boarding pass sizes, and my Mom and I spent DAYS rounding the corners and cutting out the notches! Once they were all cut out, I used a special grommet tool, and put a grommet in the corner to hold the 4 pages together. Then tied a ribbon through the grommet, inserted the boarding passes into the ticket jacket, and put them in an outer cream envelope and tied them with Raffia. For the labels, I had purchased the clear mailing labels from paperandmore.com, so I used my mail merge to print out each address, and my return address, and mailed them out! That\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s it!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> To summarize the supplies I used:<\/p> <ul> <li> 100 sheets White shimmer cardstock (<a href='http:\/\/www.paperandmore.com) \u00a066' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>www.paperandmore.com) <\/a><\/li> <\/ul> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <ul> <li> 66\u00a0sheets blue, green, aqua, coral shimmer cardstock (Archivers $0.59\/sheet, email coupons)<\/li> <\/ul> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <ul> <li> Kinkos printing and cutting services ($0.19\/print on my paper, free cutting because I batted my eyelashes <span alt=\":mswink:\" id=\"yui_3_3_0_8_130386016056263\" rel=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/msnwink.gif\"><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' height=\"19\" id=\"yui_3_3_0_8_130386016056262\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/msnwink.gif\" width=\"19\" \/><\/span><\/span><\/li> <\/ul> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <ul> <li> Wet Embossing powder in blue\/teal, and golden sand (found at Archivers for $5 each)<\/li> <\/ul> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <ul> <li> 3 stamps-Seashells, Sand, and a \u00e2\u20ac\u0153handmade with love\u00e2\u20ac\u009d stamp all found at Archivers ($7 each)<\/li> <\/ul> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <ul> <li> Embossing gun (looks like a blowdryer, but heats to ridiculous strength! Careful!<\/li> <\/ul> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <ul> <li> Last I used sticky rhinestones,\u00a0Raffia, and Ribbon\u00a0from Michaels.<\/li> <\/ul> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> This is the Boarding pass ticket jacket. Embossed with Teal\/Blue, and golden sand embossing powder (looks so real if you add a touch of teal to it!)<\/p> <p> <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394712\/width\/1000\/height\/800\"><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"Boarding pass ticket jacket 1\" height=\"343\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394712\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" width=\"476\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Another closer view of the ticket jacket.<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"Boarding pass ticket jacket 2\" height=\"332\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394714\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" style=\"width: 553px; height: 378px\" width=\"453\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> The inside of the ticket jacket.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"Inside jacket \" height=\"335\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394716\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" style=\"width: 522px; height: 359px\" width=\"443\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> The Boarding Pass itself!<\/p> <p> Page 1) Save the Date, Pack a bag\u00e2\u20ac\u00a6.<\/p> <p> Page 2) Booking information\/Travel agent information<\/p> <p> Page 3)Traveling information (passports, hotel website, dates)<\/p> <p> Page 4) Tentative RSVP \u00e2\u20ac\u201cWe\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re on board or not\u00e2\u20ac\u00a6<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"Page 1 Boarding pass STD\" height=\"356\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394719\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" style=\"width: 563px; height: 343px\" width=\"503\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> Page 2)<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"Page 2 Boarding pass STD\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394721\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Page 3)<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"Page 3 Boarding pass STD\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394723\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Page 4)<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"Page 4 Boarding pass STD\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/394725\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Okay!\u00a0 That's it for now...on to the next DIY project!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><p><span style=\"font-size:10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><strong>Azul Beach, Riviera Maya, October 22, 2011!<\/strong><\/span><\/span><\/p><span><\/span><p><span>Our website: <\/span><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/www.mikeandmandywedding.org\">http:\/\/www.mikeandmandywedding.org<\/a><\/p><span><\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"mandy.borgeson@ucdenver.edu","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1298047290,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"https:\/\/bdw-stevewright.netdna-ssl.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-236940.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":151,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"mnicole20","Id":236940,"Name":"mnicole20","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":60894,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"27a76d2fa943fdbfc9aba1bfc7ac091d","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Those came out so well!&amp;nbsp; Thanks for all the details.&amp;nbsp; I was trying to figure out how much it would cost me to make mine, and this was helpful!&amp;nbsp; Congrats!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1447777,"PostDate":1304719703,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Those came out so well!\u00a0 Thanks for all the details.\u00a0 I was trying to figure out how much it would cost me to make mine, and this was helpful!\u00a0 Congrats!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"elle.jackson@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1302031329,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"https:\/\/bdw-stevewright.netdna-ssl.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-238572.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"ellenj01","Id":238572,"Name":"ellenj01","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":60894,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"dbeb17817ef8e5ab7cb56616f48b7e30","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Very nice work...congrats! The \"we&#039;re on board\" RSVP is so cute. And thanks for the detailed information.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1447814,"PostDate":1304728473,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Very nice work...congrats! The \"we're on board\" RSVP is so cute. And thanks for the detailed information.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"pinksapphiregirl@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1304093003,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"https:\/\/bdw-stevewright.netdna-ssl.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-239459.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":237,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"redginger","Id":239459,"Name":"redginger","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":60894,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"aa28c75350b17b37e363d34e274dde50","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Thanks ladies!&amp;nbsp; I was beginning to wonder if anyone had seen my post &lt;span alt=\":D\" rel=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/cheesy.gif\"&gt;&lt;img height=\"16\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/cheesy.gif\" width=\"16\" \/&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&amp;nbsp; Glad to hear some feedback!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1448616,"PostDate":1304932483,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Thanks ladies!\u00a0 I was beginning to wonder if anyone had seen my post <span alt=\":D\" rel=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/cheesy.gif\"><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' height=\"16\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/cheesy.gif\" width=\"16\" \/><\/span><\/span>\u00a0 Glad to hear some feedback!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight